#: {{synonyms|en|backstabber}}
#* {{RQ:Alger Randy|chapter=The Iron Works Affair|page=57|passage=The trouble is, I trusted him too much from the start. He has proved to be a '''snake in the grass'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Raine Daughter of the Dons|chapter=An Optimistic Guy|page=71|passage=Is he not here to throw us out—a thief, a spy, a '''snake in the grass'''?}}
#* {{quote-song|en|author=w:Charlie Daniels|artist=Charlie Daniels|title=w:Uneasy Rider|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=w:Kama Sutra Records|month=June|year=1973|oclc=9907729|passage=He's a '''snake in the grass''', I tell you guys / He may look dumb but that's just a disguise / He's a mastermind in the ways of espionage.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:John Irving|chapter=The World According to Marcus Aurelius|title=[[w:The World According to Garp|The World According to Garp{{nb...|A Novel}}]]|series=A Henry Robbins Book|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=[[w:E. P. Dutton|E[dward] P[ayson] Dutton]]|year=1978|pages=271–272|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/worldaccordingto0000unse_v2n1/page/270/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-525-23770-9|passage=We were playing in Dallas, when that '''snake in the grass'''—Eight Ball, everyone called him—came up on my blind side&nbsp;…}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Bruce Crumley|title=Which Woman will Lead France’s Socialists?|magazine=[[w:Time (magazine)|Time]]|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20120116083204/http://www.time.com/time/world/article/0,8599,1861119,00.html|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=[[w:WarnerMedia|Time Warner Publishing]]|date=21 November 2008|issn=0928-8430|oclc=749127914|passage=Following her presidential defeat, [[w:Ségolène Royal|[Ségolène] Royal]] stunned many observers by publicly dumping Socialist Party leader {{w|François Hollande}}&nbsp;– her companion and the father of her four children&nbsp;– and announcing she'd seek his post during the current election. To some, that made Royal the symbol of the strong, modern woman in politics; to others, it cast her as the classic '''snake in the grass'''.}}

